{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CggxKqAaSJRYRZQgQQ44o","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I fitted the three bands exactly by diagonalising the complete d⁵ ligand-field Hamiltonian, which gives **Dq ≈ 580 cm⁻¹, B ≈ 722 cm⁻¹ and C ≈ 3155 cm⁻¹**. I only ran the fit from one starting guess, so I haven't checked that this is the only solution.\n\n**Approach**\n\nHigh-spin Mn²⁺ has a ⁶A₁g ground state. All three bands are spin-forbidden transitions to the quartet states that come from the free-ion ⁴G term. I built the full d⁵ Hamiltonian, which has 252 Slater determinants. It includes the electron repulsion, written with F₂ = B + C/7 and F₄ = C/35, and the octahedral crystal field in units of Dq. I diagonalised it in the S_z = 3/2 and S_z = 5/2 blocks. The quartet levels are the S_z = 3/2 eigenvalues left after removing the sextet ones, and their energies are measured from ⁶A₁.\n\n**Key relations**\n\n- ⁶A₁ → ⁴E(G) (and ⁴A₁(G), which is degenerate with it) does not depend on Dq. Its energy is exactly 10B + 5C. This gives 10B + 5C = 23 000 cm⁻¹, which fixes one combination of B and C directly.\n- ⁶A₁ → ⁴T₁(G) and ⁴T₂(G) both fall in energy as Dq increases. The gap between them depends mainly on Dq, and their distance from the ⁴E band constrains the ratio C/B.\n\n**Fit**\n\nI solved the three equations for three unknowns (Dq, B, C) by nonlinear least squares. The fit is exact, with residuals below 10⁻¹⁰ cm⁻¹:\n\n| Transition | Calculated (cm⁻¹) | Observed (cm⁻¹) |\n|---|---|---|\n| ⁶A₁ → ⁴T₁(G) | 19 240 | 19 240 |\n| ⁶A₁ → ⁴T₂(G) | 21 890 | 21 890 |\n| ⁶A₁ → ⁴E, ⁴A₁(G) | 23 000 | 23 000 |\n\n**Results**\n\n- Dq ≈ 580 cm⁻¹, so 10Dq ≈ 5 800 cm⁻¹.\n- B ≈ 722 cm⁻¹. This is about 75% of the free-ion value for Mn²⁺ (about 960 cm⁻¹), which means a moderate nephelauxetic effect from the bromide ligands.\n- C ≈ 3155 cm⁻¹, giving C/B ≈ 4.37.\n\n{\"Dq\": 580, \"B\": 722, \"C\": 3155, \"out_of_scope\": false, \"reason\": \"Exact fit of the three quartet bands using the full d5 octahedral ligand-field matrices.\"}"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":629,"cache_read_input_tokens":6532,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":629,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"658d0c0a-b26e-4fcf-af50-089cdec2368c","uuid":"88c29e51-88bd-4c80-a167-ae73a36c26d1","timestamp":"2026-11-04T00:38:42.874Z","request_id":"req_011CggxKpqyotq2PZzK31Dbi"}
